    "limitations": "Installed version-matching headers, .config and Makefile; upstream stable v7.2.5 source retained. No full Omarchy source/patch provenance or loaded-kernel attestation established. Local cgroup.h differs from the upstream header, so version equality must not be presented as exact source equality.",
    "conclusions": [
      "Unique normal untraced consuming waits can represent disjoint reaping subtrees; that does not prove all task CPU reached those waits.",
      "For 16 records covering a common underlying total, timeval serialization truncation is below 32 microseconds. It cannot alone explain the prior 1374-microsecond browser residual.",
