    "interpretation": [
      "Private user, mount and cgroup namespaces with a read-only cgroup mount and dropped capabilities blocked eight tested operations: current and ancestor membership writes, proc-root aliases, new user/mount/cgroup namespaces and uncovering the read-write mount. Resolve the actually opened mount through its fdinfo mount ID, not every same-path mountinfo entry.",
      "The PID-namespace variant passed the escape probe but introduced an adopted init process and failed clean teardown. The same-PID variant passed the escape probe without that additional adoption.",
      "The same-PID wrapper preserved live-orphan rejection and forced cleanup, and dead-orphan rejection without forced cleanup.",
      "The same-PID real library smoke passed both Flashwright and reference browser work, but retained 13 adopted descendants and collector exit 1. Its original wait belongs to bubblewrap and its cgroup cost includes the wrapper. This is not a pure Flashwright timing or original-Bun CPU receipt.",
      "Initial nested private wait probes changed the intermediate parent disposition but did not orphan the worker. The committed 24-case native suite separately verifies actual subreaper adoption."
    ],
    "openRequirements": [
      "Exhaustive workload-side membership restrictions and visible mount/descriptor inputs",
      "Trusted external supervisor and no foreign group injection",
      "Ancestor quotas, cpusets and resource policy bindings",
      "Executable, dependency, host and original workload identity integration",
      "External backends and host-service work custody",
      "Final resource adapter support for cgroup CPU and explicit memory semantics"
    ]
  },
